  "worked_solution": "The elements of the given set are the positive real numbers that satisfy the inequality ${x}^{2}-1\\le 15.$ \n\nSo, we first need to solve our inequality for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & \\le 15 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\le 16 \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\le \\sqrt{16} \\\\ |x| & \\le 4 \\\\ -4\\le x & \\le 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe positive real numbers that are solutions to the inequality above are $x\\in (0,4].$ Therefore, the given set can be written as \n\n$$\nA=(0,4].\n$$",
